Retain unknown bitmap coverage. Untagged multiple known segments keep all effectively nonempty segments, or oldest if all empty; a sole known empty segment remains. Tagged history preserves all same-name coverage segments, including retired source IDs and empty definitions. Missing schema fields still remove ordinary indices before the tagged branch. This changes metadata membership without rewriting stored bitmap provenance or deleting files. (rust/lance-table/src/transaction/index_maintenance.rs:517-625)

TaggedLineage stores two independent kinds of knowledge: coverage bitmap and usable ledger. contains() treats absent bitmap as possible membership; mentions()/destination walks return None without ledger. Known leaf destinations are Some(empty), which must not be collapsed into unknown. Unsupported transitions disable the supplied ledger; absent prefetched external history errors in from_indices_with_ledger. (rust/lance-table/src/system_index/frag_reuse/lineage.rs:23-140)



